#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fx: the deterministic half of the software factory.

The /auto-factory:code skill (an LLM) decides *what to ask agents*; this script owns
everything that must not drift: job state and legal stage moves, model routing
(never below Sonnet), the gate, Jira reads/writes and pull requests.

The factory never lives inside a project. Each project has its own factory
repository (factory.json, checks.sh, knowledge/, lessons.md; jobs/ stays local),
created by `fx init --project <git URL>`. Code is worked on in throw-away clones
under the work folder next to it: one clone per job, deleted once its branch is
pushed, and short-lived clones for reading. Standard library only, Python 3.9+.
Run it from the factory repository:
    python3 <skill dir>/fx <command> ...

Every command prints a JSON object on stdout (human hints go to stderr) and
exits non-zero on failure, so the orchestrator can follow `next` blindly.
"""

